<div align="center">

# Argus

**A see-through desktop overlay for your second monitor.**

Browser · Discord · Steam · Spotify · Files by size · System stats · Weather · Calendar · Clipboard

[**Download v0.9.0 (beta)**](https://github.com/Neks-Git/Argus/releases/tag/v0.9.0)

</div>

---

## what it is

One transparent window with glassy tiles for the stuff you actually look at. The gaps between tiles are really see-through — your wallpaper shows and clicks pass through to whatever's behind.

![](homess.png)

**Screenshots:** [system stats](statsss.png) · [spotify](spotifyss.png) · [steam](steamss.png) · [browser](browserss.png)

---

## install

**1.** Download [`Argus-0.9.0.zip`](https://github.com/Neks-Git/Argus/releases/tag/v0.9.0) from the release page and extract it.

**2.** Run `Argus Setup 0.9.0.exe`.

> **Windows will prob warn you** — "Windows protected your PC." That's because the exe is unsigned, not because it's suspicious. Click **More info** → **Run anyway**. [Why this happens and how to verify the app →](Argus_%20READMEACTUALLYREADME.html)

**3.** If the installer asks, pick **"just me"** — this keeps `config.json` in a folder you can edit without admin rights.

**4.** Launch Argus. It works immediately — browser, discord, steam, files, stats, weather, calendar, clipboard, all fine with no setup.

---

## hotkeys

| keys | what |
|---|---|
| `Ctrl+Alt+Space` | hide / show Argus |
| `Ctrl+Alt+F` | toggle fill-screen |
| `Ctrl+Alt+V` | open clipboard history |

All three are rebindable in `config.json`.

---

## optional: connect spotify and steam

Everything works out of the box. These two add extra functionality.

### Spotify (playback controls, playlists, now-playing tile)

1. Create a free app at [developer.spotify.com/dashboard](https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard)
2. Add `http://127.0.0.1:8888/callback` as a redirect URI (exact match)
3. Copy the **client ID** into `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\argus\config.json`:
   ```json
   "spotifyClientId": "your-client-id-here"
